  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "Prior to the commencement of the development (excluding demolition works), full details of the secure cycle storage facilities shall be submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority which shall show their positioning within the site, the size and materials of the enclosure and the means of access. The approved details shall be implemented on site prior to the first occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter permanently retained in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure the development provides an adequate level of cycle parking facilities and to encourage sustainable modes of transport, in accordance with policies 36 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended) (or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), prior to the first occupation of the premises for a use within Class E(d) (indoor sport, recreation, or fitness) or Class E(f) (day nursery, crèche, or day centre), details of the proposed hours of use and noise mitigation measures (including acoustic insulation and ventilation), demonstrating no unacceptable adverse impact on residential amenity, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The use shall only commence in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To enable the Local Planning Authority to assess the specific impacts of high-intensity uses on the amenity and living conditions of the occupiers of neighbouring residential properties, particularly those within the upper floors of the application building in accordance with SLP Policy 29.",
    "The use hereby permitted (Class E or Sui Generis) shall only take place between the hours of 08:00 and midnight Monday to Sunday.\r\rReason: To provide certainty and safeguard the living conditions of surrounding residential occupiers (in accordance with SLP Policy 29).",
    "Service vehicle deliveries/collections to and from the unit hereby permitted shall only take place between the hours of: 08:00 to 22:00 Monday to Saturday and 09:00 to 20:00 on Sundays and Bank/Public Holidays.\r\rReason: To safeguard the living conditions of surrounding residential occupiers from unreasonable disturbance (in accordance with SLP Policy 29).",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08.00 and 18.00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08.00 and 13.00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of surrounding occupiers in line with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the approved Fire Safety Strategy (Part A) Reasonable Exception Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
